From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:58:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): comment on labelled items and submit the comments
 together

Reviewing what an agent raised as labelled items ([Q2], [R1], ...) usually
means answering several of them at once. Typing one long reply by hand loses
the structure: the agent has to work out which paragraph answers which item,
and nothing ties the answer back to the item afterwards. Commenting on each
item and submitting them together, like reviewing a document, keeps both.

Clicking a chip (in a message, in the Open items panel, or the label in its
own defining message, which is now clickable) opens the item popover, which
gains a Comment button. Comment switches the real composer into comment mode
for that item: a header card names it, and whatever was typed is set aside
until the comment is saved, so attachments, paste, @-mentions and dictation
work as usual. Enter or the check button saves the comment to a drafts tray
above the composer, styled like the queued-messages strip; it can be
minimized to one line, and drafts can be edited or deleted (with undo).
Chips with unsent drafts show an amber dot, chips with sent comments a count.

Submit comments (N) in the action row sends every draft as one plain-markdown
user message through the normal send path, so it queues like any message
while the agent is busy (the queue row reads "3 comments on Q2 R1"). A
message typed in the composer goes along as a General section. The format:

  Comments on 2 items:

  #### [Q2] <item title>

  **1.** <comment>

  **2.** <comment>

  Attachments: q2-1.png

  #### [R1] <item title>

  <comment>

  #### General

  <typed message>

Sections follow the order the items were defined; comments are numbered only
when an item has several; headings inside a comment are demoted to bold;
attached files are real file blocks, renamed to be unique within the message
(a pasted image.png on Q2 becomes q2-1.png) and listed by name, since native
harnesses drop file blocks on the transcript round trip.

Sent comments are not stored anywhere new: the label index parses the
sections back out of user messages, and the popover lists each comment with
its files and the first sentence about the item in the next agent message,
on any device and after any reload. A comment heading counts as a mention but
leaves an item open or closed; a plain mention still reopens it.

Drafts live in this browser only: localStorage keyed by session, synced
between tabs with the storage event, with attachment bytes in IndexedDB so
they survive a reload. Submitted drafts are kept, marked as sent, until the
message posts; cancelling or editing the queued message, a failed send, or a
page closed while it waited in the in-memory queue puts them back as drafts.

Web only; no server, protocol or schema change.

It also adds the reply rule to the item-label instruction every agent gets
(omnigent/runtime/prompt.py): answer each commented item by its label, and a
comment on a closed item does not reopen it.

Not upstream yet: to be proposed together with the labelled-items renderer;
drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
